description:
Found by an audit of the whole set on 2026-09-25, after the owner twice called a fix "too literal" (0.57.2 rule retold issue #8; 2026-09-23 design-question rule copied one session's list).

## What happened
Fixes accumulated as retellings of the sessions that prompted them instead of the general pattern:
- rules carrying one incident's details: quoted excuses, counts ("four of them in a row"), one conversation's lists, one tool's or one tracker's quirks, a grading scale from one experiment;
- one pattern written as several rules (read the record not memory, about seven places; a given decision is acted on, four; work made obsolete by another decision, three; list order, four; show an instance, two; three timeout rules that contradict on overrun);
- skills restating protocol rules instead of citing them, and rules invented in two skills that the protocol lacks (lessons that outlive the work, a worker commits only its own paths);
- established practices described in homemade words (Goodhart's law, watchdog, shift-left, sunk cost, reference-class forecasting, controlled experiment, rule of three, fail fast, de-identification);
- setup-free skills copying "keeping needs a task" because Tracked work and Exploration is not admission live in protocol.md, which they may not link.

## What was expected
Each rule states the pattern once, names its discipline, sits in one reference and is cited by name; a skill keeps only its own step, timing and trigger.
